# Structure and Naming Rules

> Full architecture: `docs/architecture.md`

## Where code lives

- **Domain features:** `src/modules/{domain}/`
  - `controllers/` — HTTP (admin/buyer/seller/public prefixes)
  - `application/commands/` — mutations
  - `application/queries/` — reads / list DTOs
  - `domain/` — entities, enums, policies
  - `repositories/` — only Drizzle access
  - `dto/`, `mappers/`
- **Infrastructure:** `src/libs/` (guards, email, config, events — no domain rules)
- **DB transaction types:** `@/libs/db/types` (`DrizzleTx`, `TLockTransaction`)
- **Schema:** `src/_db/drizzle/schema/{domain}/` — repos in owning module only

## Legacy paths (removed)

Do **not** reintroduce `src/api/`, `src/_repositories/`, or `src/common/`. See `docs/REFACTOR_COMPLETE.md`.

## Naming

- `*.controller.ts`, `*.module.ts`
- Commands: `place-order.command.ts`, `cancel-order.command.ts`
- Queries: `get-buyer-orders.query.ts`, `list-admin-orders.query.ts`
- `dto/*.dto.ts`
- Repositories: `{aggregate}.repository.ts` (aggregate-level, not per-table)

## Reuse

Reuse existing helpers in `src/libs/` before creating duplicates.

## Tests

Colocate tests under `__tests__/unit|integration|fixtures` in the same folder as the code under test — not beside production files. See `60-testing-and-done-criteria.mdc`.
